# The `lite` edition: a usable hacking + coding workstation inside a 4 GB,
# 2-vCPU guest. Sized for old laptops (a dual-core i5 MacBook Air, say) where
# the host also needs to stay responsive.
#
# What is deliberately NOT here: Ghidra and Cutter (JVM/Qt, want 4 GB to
# themselves), the whole gaming stack, Docker and libvirt, Chromium, GIMP,
# OBS, VS Code. Add any of them later with pacman; nothing stops you.

# coding
git
base-devel
python
python-pip
python-virtualenv
python-requests
neovim
tmux
jq
ripgrep
fd
fzf
bat
htop
unzip
7zip
wget
curl
man-db

# recon and scanning
nmap
whois
bind
arp-scan
gobuster
# ffuf is AUR-only: undrabyte-toolkit aur ffuf (or BlackArch's copy)

# traffic
wireshark-cli
tcpdump
mitmproxy
socat
openbsd-netcat
sshuttle

# web and exploitation
sqlmap
impacket
# metasploit and exploitdb are the two heaviest tools (~300 MB together) and
# are left out of `lite` to keep the ISO under GitHub's 2 GiB download limit.
# Install them on demand:  sudo pacman -S metasploit exploitdb
# The full/security/dev editions still bake them in.

# passwords
john
hydra

# reversing (CLI only - no GUI disassembler at this size)
radare2
binwalk

# tunnelling
proxychains-ng
tor
torsocks
openvpn
wireguard-tools

# scripting
python-scapy

# light browser + editor for the desktop
firefox
keepassxc
